            <ArticleTitle>[The state of children in the early period after adenectomy].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>58-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Sixty-three children, aged 3 to 12, were examined after adenotomy made with general anesthesia. The parameters of central hemodynamics and of cardiointervalography describing the state of the vegetative nervous system as well as the postoperative clinical course were analyzed in children after adenotomy. A high sympathoadrenal activity with a trend to reduction was noted in children immediately after adenotomy. The psycho-emotional state and the postoperative pain severity got back to the normal values within 1 postoperative hour.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
